# commit b0b24bfaba153566cd895864d8c123e556ab035f 2026-11-17 "T-0154: inkcmp lines step 2a, side stamps: rotated text in a lane at the page's edge (arXiv's identifier) is found on the grey page (it is grey 127, lighter than the page threshold), erased from the ink, and emitted as one page_info record with its rotation (IcLine.rot: 90 bottom-to-top, 270 top-to-bottom, from the densest column across the lane); a lane is a stamp when >= 50% of its rows hold ink (stamps 74.5% / 78.7%, a line-number column 22.5%); gd3-bands reads the rot field"
